    <string name="help_dialog_title">Help</string>
    <string name="help_dialog_detail">
        \n** If the input method misbehaves, try the [Reset settings] function at the bottom left to clear data and settings.\n
        \nRelease notes (2026.06.01 - Tablet flagship upgrade)\n
        1. [Physical keyboard] Dayi left-side paging: a fixed page up/down panel (▲/▼) on the far left for physical keyboard users, so you can page with the left hand and type with the right. The buttons use a high-contrast teal when available and are disabled when there are no more pages to prevent mistaps.\n
        2. [UI] Full-screen immersive console: the traditional title bar is hidden so the console extends edge to edge for maximum visible area.\n
        3. [Visual] Card-based settings and AI status light: all settings are grouped into rounded cards. Dayi smart selection shows a green/grey \"learning status\" breathing light to indicate its state.\n
        4. [Layout] Integrated toolbar: [Help] and [Reset settings] are neatly placed at the bottom of the left sidebar.\n\n
        \nRelease notes (2026.02.28)\n
        1. [Removed] Voice input: removed the voice input key, VoiceInputActivity and related resources to simplify the input method framework.\n
        2. [Tests] Unit tests: 30 cases for LimeDB table name validation, 17 cases for IMSwitchHelper switching logic and 19 cases for OptionsDialogHelper menus, 66 test cases in total, all passing.\n\n
        \nRelease notes (2026.02.05)\n
        1. Emoji keyboard fix (Emoji Picker): fixed the emoji keyboard failing to show or interrupting input when switched to while typing.\n
        2. System optimization: improved input method startup stability and code integration.\n\n
        \nRelease notes (2026.01.03)\n
        1. UI modernization: adopted Material Design 3 throughout, with dynamic color and edge-to-edge display.\n
        2. Tablet support: fixed locked screen orientation and added support for landscape split mode.\n
        3. System optimization: removed ads, cloud backup and sharing to improve performance and security.\n
        4. Crash fix: fixed a crash caused by the side menu (Navigation Drawer).\n
        5. Version format change: versions now use the date format (yyyy.MM.dd) for easier identification.\n\n
        Thanks to the inventor of the Dayi input method and its sponsors. LIME is officially licensed to use it.\n\n
    </string>
